#basePath	Day1


:: OpeningCutscene
@trigger SceneReady
@who    IntroCutscene

$call SetInputState(false)
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling", 1)
$call IntroCutscene->BeginCutscene()
$call Wait(2)
$call TelescopeLook(155, -30)

:: ArrivalAtTheShed
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "IntroCutscene"
@who    Radio

$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling-Piano", 1)
{@Astrid} Whoa. This place has really changed.
Elijah, where are you?

$call Wait(2)

{@Radio} Star HQ to Station Seven. Elijah, do you copy?
$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} Please log in and provide status update. 

$call Wait(2)

{@Astrid} Hi—um, this is Astrid, Elijah’s ... friend. Elijah’s not here.
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Hello?
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Ugh. They can’t hear me.
$call Wait(2)

{@Radio} Station Seven, please log in and report.

$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid} I can’t, I don’t know how ...

$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} I told you, he's not there... Astrid?
$call Wait(1)
Is that you?

{@Astrid} (*gasp*) Dad! I can’t believe it's you.
Are you still at the South Pole? Are you okay?
$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} This is a one-way radio, so you won’t be able to talk to us. But I have a feeling that’s you. Happy birthday, kiddo. 
I heard from your aunt Martha that you managed to track down Elijah’s address.
I’m sorry, Astrid ... I wish I could’ve warned you in time. 
Elijah’s not there. He probably won’t be back for a while.

$call Wait(2)

{@Astrid} What? 
$call Wait(1)
Why not? 
$call Wait(1)
Where is he? 
$call Wait(2)
Ugh, forgot ... you can’t hear me. 
$call Wait(2)

{@Dad} There’s not much time, so I’ll give you the short version.
My team here at IceCube has started an underground group called the STAR Coalition. We’re trying to rebuild our knowledge of the night sky. 
$call Wait(1)
It’s not easy ... so much was lost during the Collapse.
$call Wait(1)
But then Elijah reached out to us. He’s onto something big...

{@Astrid} Onto what?

{@Dad} I'm so glad you're there though. We could really use your help.

{@Astrid} As if I know how any of this stuff works...

{@Dad} I know you aren't familiar with most of that equipment, but I'll walk you through the basics.
Don't worry about clerance for the more advanced equipment, that will come in time... if you're up for it. 
First things first, we you need to submit some data the old fashioned way.
Sending you the data now...

$call WaitForMovedToView("Monitor")
(*neutrino upload noises*)

{@Dad} OK, looks like you received the coordinates. 
{@Dad} See if you can move your telescope.

$call SetInputState(true)
$call StopMusic(2)
$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("TelescopeControls", 0.4)
$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = false
$goto .MoveTelescopeReminder

:: MoveTelescopeReminder
$call Wait(10)
$if !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
    {@Dad} Still there?
     See if you can move your telescope.
    $goto .MoveTelescopeReminder
$endif
// //TODO Shake UI hint

:: MoveYourTelescope
@trigger    OnTelescopeMoved
@when   !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
@interrupt
@once

$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = true
$call HintModals->Hide("TelescopeControls", 0.2)
Nice job! Your equipment seems to be working.

$call Wait(2)

See those three lights above your monitor? Feel up for a game of hot an cold?
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("NeutrinoNav", 0.4)

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@once

{@Dad} Nice Job! 
Early this morning, Ice Cube detected a high energy neutrino coming from one of several possible stars in this location.
You’ll see each of them highlighted on your display. 
Identifying these stars will be a great way for you get your feet wet and upgrade your system.
$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
$call StartOpenMode()

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@once

$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
{@Dad}
Looks like you’ve identified enough stars to earn a higher clearance level. 
You’ll need to tune to the right frequency on your radio to unlock your equipment. Tune to 375mHz.

{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 2. 
You are now cleared to use the color meter. 
Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment. 

Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. 
Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow.

{@Astrid} Huh...

{@Radio} Tuning you to the Ice Cube CERES headquarters for further instruction...

{@Dad} Awesome, your rig is upgraded! 
This time I need you to find the constellation Perseus.

{@Astrid} Perseus, huh?

{@Dad} Up for some more hot and cold?
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
{@Radio} This task will require your astral color instrument. 
{@Radio} Unlocking now. Stand By...
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
$call StartPuzzleMode()

:: PerseusPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Perseus"
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Time to turn in for the night.
Oh, what's this?
$call WaitForMovedToView("Left")
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day1Martha")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: EndDay
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day1Martha"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call LoadNextDay()